WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Moderator: Tell me about the last time you got ready for a customer check-in.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Priya Raman: I manage about thirty enterprise accounts, so before every check-in I open the Customer 360 and look at the health score first. If it's red I know what kind of call it's going to be.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Priya Raman: But honestly I don't trust the health score. It's a number, and I can't see why it changed. Last month one of my best accounts dropped twenty points and I had no idea what caused it.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Moderator: What did you do when that happened?

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:39.000
Priya Raman: I opened five tabs. Usage in one, tickets in another, billing in a third, then my own notes in a spreadsheet. It took forty minutes to find out the drop was just a billing contact who left.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:02:03.000
Priya Raman: The timeline in the Customer 360 is the one thing I love. Seeing every email, ticket and call in order saves me a ton of time.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Moderator: Where does it fall short?

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:39.000
Priya Raman: The data is stale. Usage sometimes lags by two days, so I walk into a call and the customer tells me something I should have already seen.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:03:07.000
Priya Raman: And when a customer escalates to support I lose the thread. Support closes the ticket, and I only find out when the customer mentions it. The handoff is basically an email.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:26.000
Moderator: How do you hear about risk early?

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:47.000
Priya Raman: The risk alerts are too noisy. I get twenty a day and maybe two matter. So I started ignoring them, which is dangerous, and then I find out a renewal is at risk when it's already late.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:14.000
Priya Raman: What I'd want is a plain explanation next to the score. Something like: usage down thirty percent, two escalations in the last month, champion left. Then I'd trust it.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:41.000
Priya Raman: Renewals are the other pain. Preparing for one means pulling a usage report, the contract, the open tickets and last quarter's notes, all in different places.

